date-released: "2026-10-10"
# doi: [ZENODO_DOI]   <- uncomment and fill in after the first Zenodo release (a bracket placeholder is not a valid DOI)
repository-code: "https://github.com/AutoDrops/asm-eval"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Evaluation results and a standalone scoring script for ASM, a compact state memory for long-running LLM agents
  (implementation not included). On the internal closed set c3 (216 questions per method) ASM scored 85.6% vs 72.7%
  for full history with about 12.6x less context. On a 100-question stratified subset of the LongMemEval ORACLE
  variant (not the official 500-question result) ASM scored 49% vs 58% for BM25 and 66% for full history.
  Preliminary study, not independently reproduced.
keywords:
  - LLM agents
  - long-term memory
  - evaluation
  - LongMemEval
